### 2. Create the `index.php` file
This file will handle the HTTP POST request and insert the data into the database.

```php
<!-- index.php -->
<?php
require_once 'db.php';

// Check if the request is POST and fields are set
if ($_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] === 'POST' && isset($_POST['field1'], $_POST['field2'])) {
    $field1 = $_POST['field1'];
    $field2 = $_POST['field2'];

    // Prepare and bind
    $stmt = $conn->prepare("INSERT INTO your_table_name (field1, field2) VALUES (?, ?)");
    $stmt->bind_param("ss", $field1, $field2);

    // Execute the statement
    if ($stmt->execute()) {
        echo "New record created successfully";
    } else {
        echo "Error: " . $stmt->error;
    }

    // Close the statement
    $stmt->close();
} else {
