   - If the number of rated players `X` is less than `N`, then the maximum number of rated players who can be paired with unrated players is `X`. The remaining rated players will have to pair with other rated players.
   - If `X` is greater than or equal to `N`, then all `N` rated players can be paired with unrated players, and the remaining `X - N` rated players will have to pair with other rated players. The number of such pairs will be `2 * N - 2 * X`.

