user prompt:
I'm having trouble with css. I have two buttons in a parent container and I want one to be left aligned and the other right aligned but using flex for responsive reasons.

response:
Certainly! You can achieve left and right alignment of two buttons within a parent container using CSS Flexbox. Here's a simple example to help you get started:

### HTML
```html
<div class="container">
    <button class="left-button">Left Button</button>
    <button class="right-button">Right Button</button>
</div>
```

### CSS
```css
.container {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between; /* This will push the buttons to opposite ends */
    align-items: center; /* Aligns the buttons vertically in the center */
    padding: 10px; /* Optional: adds some padding for spacing */
    border: 1px solid #ccc; /* Optional: adds a border for visual separation */
}

.left-button {
    margin-right: 10px; /* Optional: adds some space between the buttons */
}

.right-button {
    margin-left: 10px; /* Optional: adds some space between the buttons */
}
```

### Explanation:
- **`.container`**: This is the parent container where both buttons will be placed. The `display: flex;` property makes the container a flex container.
- **`justify-content: space-between;`**: This property will distribute the buttons to the far ends of the container. The buttons will be pushed away from each other.
- **`align-items: center;`**: This will vertically center the buttons within the container (if you want to align them differently, you can change this).
- **Optional Margins**: The `margin-right` and `margin-left` classes are optional and can be used to add spacing between the buttons, if needed.

### Example Output:
- The `Left Button` will be aligned to the left edge of the container.
- The `Right Button` will be aligned to the right edge of the container.
- There will be space between the buttons (if you add the optional margin classes).

Feel free to adjust the styles as needed for your specific use case!
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
