index = scale_to_index(score)
print(f"Score: {score}, Index: {index}")

score = 7
index = scale_to_index(score)
print(f"Score: {score}, Index: {index}")

score = 4
index = scale_to_index(score)
print(f"Score: {score}, Index: {index}")
```

This function works as follows:
- When the score is 1, the index is \((7 - 1) / 6 = 1\).
- When the score is 7, the index is \((7 - 7) / 6 = 0\).
- For any score in between, the index is calculated proportionally.

You can test the function with different scores to see how it maps to the new index scale.
