The ring of integers in \( \mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{-11}) \) is \( \mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-11}] \), which is the set of all numbers of the form \( a + b\sqrt{-11} \) with \( a, b \in \mathbb{Z} \).

