2. **Redirects and Authentication**: Sometimes, the URL might redirect to a login page before finally downloading the file. If your script doesn't handle these redirects, it might not be able to reach the final download URL.

3. ** headers**: Some websites require specific headers to be passed in the request, such as `User-Agent`, which can help the server identify the request as coming from a web browser.

To address these issues, you can use a more robust HTTP client like `requests.Session()` to handle cookies and redirects, and you can also set the `User-Agent` header.

Here's an updated version of your script:

```python
import requests
from requests.auth import HTTPBasicAuth

# Main Power BI report URL
full_url = "https://app.powerbi.com/groups/me/rdlreports/1bdef01c-30a3-4150-aff2-b3ec4c9edf86?rp:AdviceDeathScriptMERGEDMonthStartDate=6/1/2023&rp:AdviceDeathScriptMERGEDIncomingcall=Aria%20Park&rdl:format=PDF"

# Session to handle cookies and redirects
session = requests.Session()

# Set User-Agent header
headers = {
    'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/58.0.3029.110 Safari/537.3'}

# Get the initial page to set the cookies and handle redirects
