\]

### (c) Probability that they meet in any round

To find the probability that the two chosen players meet in any round, we need to consider the total number of matches across all rounds. The total number of matches in a knock-out tournament with \(2^n\) players is \(2^n - 1\) (since each match eliminates one player and we need \(2^n - 1\) eliminations to determine a winner).

The probability that the two chosen players meet in any round is the ratio of the total number of matches to the total number of ways to choose 2 players:

