\[
\ket{\psi} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} \left( \ket{00} + \ket{01} + \ket{10} \right)
\]

Next, we compute \(\bra{\psi}\):

\[
\bra{\psi} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} \left( \bra{00} + \bra{01} + \bra{10} \right)
\]

Now, we calculate \(\rho\):

\[
\rho = \frac{1}{3} \left( \ket{00} + \ket{01} + \ket{10} \right) \left( \bra{00} + \bra{01} + \bra{10} \right)
\]

Expanding this, we get:

\[
\rho = \frac{1}{3} \left( \ket{00} \bra{00} + \ket{00} \bra{01} + \ket{00} \bra{10} + \ket{01} \bra{00} + \ket{01} \bra{01} + \ket{01} \bra{10} + \ket{10} \bra{00} + \ket{10} \bra{01} + \ket{10} \bra{10} \right)
\]

We now collect the terms involving the second qubit:

\[
\rho = \frac{1}{3} \left( \ket{00} \bra{00} + \ket{01} \bra{01} + \ket{10} \bra{10} \right) + \frac{1}{3} \left( \ket{00} \bra{01} + \ket{01} \bra{00} \right) + \frac{1}{3} \left( \ket{00} \bra{10} + \ket{10} \bra{00} \right) + \frac{1}{3} \left( \ket{01} \bra{10} + \ket{10} \bra{01} \right)
\]

To find the reduced density matrix of the second qubit, we take the partial trace over the first qubit. This means we sum over the basis states of the first qubit. The reduced density matrix \(\rho_2\) is given by:

\[
\rho_2 = \text{Tr}_1(\rho)
\]

We need to trace out the first qubit's contributions:

\[
\rho_2 = \frac{1}{3} \left( \text{Tr}_1(\ket{00} \bra{00}) + \text{Tr}_1(\ket{01} \bra{01}) + \text{Tr}_1(\ket{10} \bra{10}) \right)
\]

